{"id": "word-meaning", "seconds": 4.547, "reply": {"type": "turn.result", "id": "word-meaning", "kind": "conversation", "operation": null, "intentOperations": [], "effectOperations": [], "question": "", "reply": "Desmutear significa hacer que alguien vuelva a poder escuchar o comunicarse, especialmente en contextos como redes sociales o aplicaciones de mensajer\u00eda, donde antes estaban silenciados o desactivados. Si est\u00e1s en un grupo o chat, desmutear te permite escuchar los mensajes o voces de los dem\u00e1s nuevamente.", "conversationKind": "knowledge", "responseLanguage": "es", "turn_attempts": 1}}
{"id": "definition-en", "seconds": 0.641, "reply": {"type": "turn.result", "id": "definition-en", "kind": "conversation", "operation": null, "intentOperations": [], "effectOperations": [], "question": "", "reply": "Unmute means to turn on the microphone so you can speak or be heard in a conversation or meeting.", "conversationKind": "knowledge", "preserveObjective": false, "responseLanguage": "en", "turn_attempts": 1}}
{"id": "ram-new-topic", "seconds": 1.468, "reply": {"type": "turn.result", "id": "ram-new-topic", "kind": "conversation", "operation": null, "intentOperations": [], "effectOperations": [], "question": "", "reply": "RAM is short for Random Access Memory \u2014 it's the temporary storage that your computer uses to quickly access and process data while running programs. Think of it like a workspace: when you're working on a document or playing a game, the data you're using is stored in RAM so your computer can access it fast. The more RAM you have, the more programs you can run at once without slowing down.", "conversationKind": "knowledge", "preserveObjective": false, "responseLanguage": "en", "turn_attempts": 1}}
